# Every variant of the env file, not only the canonical name.
#
# `.env` alone was ignored, so the backups `set-secrets.sh` and a dozen manual
# edits leave behind — .env.bak.20260913-015342 and its siblings — showed up
# as untracked files on the production box. Each one holds the JWT secret, the
# token encryption key, the Anthropic key and a live Paystack secret in
# plaintext, and a single `git add -A` on that server would have committed all
# of them. A secret in git history is a secret that has to be rotated, not
# deleted.
.env.*
!.env.example
